  "claim_short": "The open problem in arXiv:2108.12798 asks for rank D_2(T) for an arbitrary tree. Ali Azimi and Sivaramakrishnan Sivasubramanian, The 2-Steiner distance matrix of a tree, Linear Algebra and its Applications 655 (2022), Theorem 1, proves that for every tree T on n vertices with p pendant vertices, rank D_2(T)=2n-p-1. This exactly extends the source's caterpillar formula and fully resolves the question.",
